{"event": "report", "t": 1795202478.426, "claim": "fixed", "verdict": {"verdict": "fixed", "root_cause": {"category": "logic", "model": "rpt_category_performance", "summary": "The model drives from products with LEFT joins to product_variants and order_lines, so every product that never sold produced a (category, NULL month) row. Those rows inflated unique_products for categories with no sales (SERVICE 6, DIGITAL 8, GIFT_CARD 2 unsold products were counted) and created bogus null-month rows. Revenue, units, orders and gross profit totals were unaffected because those rows carried NULL/zero values."}, "evidence": [{"kind": "lineage", "ref": "models/marts/product/rpt_category_performance.sql", "finding": "FROM products p with LEFT JOIN product_variants and LEFT JOIN order_lines lets products without any sales produce rows with NULL sales_month."}, {"kind": "query", "ref": "rpt_category_performance WHERE sales_month IS NULL (before fix)", "finding": "Four null-month rows: SERVICE (unique_products 6), DIGITAL (8), GIFT_CARD (2), all with NULL revenue and 0 orders, plus PHYSICAL orphan-line row. The unsold-product rows are spurious."}, {"kind": "query", "ref": "source totals vs mart (before fix)", "finding": "SUM(line_total) in stg_orders__order_lines = 722313.24 equals SUM(revenue) in mart; units 6590 match. No fan-out in revenue or units."}, {"kind": "query", "ref": "direct recomputation by category and month", "finding": "Direct aggregation from order_lines->variants->products->orders matched the mart on revenue, units and orders for every group that has sales; the only mismatches were the three unsold-product null-month rows."}, {"kind": "query", "ref": "grain checks on staging tables", "finding": "product_id, variant_id, order_line_id and order_id are unique in their staging tables, so the joins do not fan out."}, {"kind": "query", "ref": "rpt_category_performance after fix", "finding": "199 rows (was 202); revenue 722313.24, units 6590, gross profit 608293.75, orders 2217 unchanged; one null-month row remains (see caveat)."}], "changes": [{"path": "models/marts/product/rpt_category_performance.sql", "summary": "Changed the product-to-variant and variant-to-order-line joins from LEFT to INNER so only products with sold order lines feed the report. This removes the spurious unsold-product rows and corrects unique_products. Columns, grain (category x month) and materialisation (view) are unchanged."}], "confidence": "medium"}, "diffs": [{"path": "models/marts/product/rpt_category_performance.sql", "diff": "--- a/models/marts/product/rpt_category_performance.sql\n+++ b/models/marts/product/rpt_category_performance.sql\n@@ -27,7 +27,7 @@\n     avg(ol.unit_price) as avg_unit_price,\n     sum(ol.line_total) - sum(ol.quantity_ordered * pv.cost_price) as gross_profit\n from products p\n-left join product_variants pv on p.product_id = pv.product_id\n-left join order_lines ol on pv.variant_id = ol.variant_id\n+inner join product_variants pv on p.product_id = pv.product_id\n+inner join order_lines ol on pv.variant_id = ol.variant_id\n left join orders o on ol.order_id = o.order_id\n group by 1, 2\n"}], "text": "The verifier accepted the fix. The run is over.\n\n**Root cause:** `rpt_category_performance` starts from `products` and uses LEFT joins to `product_variants` and `order_lines`. Every product that never sold therefore produced a row with a NULL sales month. Those rows inflated `unique_products` for categories with no sales: SERVICE counted 6 unsold products, DIGITAL 8 and GIFT_CARD 2. Revenue, units, orders and gross profit were not affected, because those rows carried NULL or zero values.\n\n**Change:** In `models/marts/product/rpt_category_performance.sql`, I changed the `product_variants` and `order_lines` joins from LEFT to INNER. Columns, grain (category \u00d7 month) and the view materialisation are unchanged.\n\n**Checks:**\n- Revenue (722,313.24), units (6,590), gross profit (608,293.75) and orders (2,217) are the same before and after the fix.\n- Recomputing revenue, units and orders directly from the staging tables matched the mart for every group that has sales.\n- Row count fell from 202 to 199, which is the three unsold-product rows removed.\n- `run_dbt` on the model passed.\n\n**Left open:** One NULL-month row remains. It is PHYSICAL revenue of about 2,950 from 18 order lines whose `order_id` has no header in `stg_orders__orders`. That is a source referential problem, and I did not filter it out. Also, `dbt build` as a whole still fails on an unrelated seed. `seeds/product_categories.csv` collides with an existing `PRODUCT_CATEGORIES` view, and about 120 staging tests fail. I did not touch either, since they are outside this model.\n\n**Confidence:** medium. The verifier passed the fix, but whether the unsold-product rows should be excluded is a judgment call about what the report is meant to count."}
